                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[quote][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/9686972/]Follow \"[b]First Person Exploration and Puzzle Games[/b]\" for more games like this![/url][/quote]\n\nThis developer made several lateral-thinking puzzle games that I enjoyed [i](most notably [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/2013650/Logicality/?curator_clanid=39661507]Logicality[/url], a lateral-thinking game based on The Witness)[/i], so I was looking forward to this one.  Unfortunately it's a complete letdown.\n\nThe game starts out by asking you to press one of three buttons.  If you press the wrong one, the ceiling comes down and kills you. There are no hints indicating which button to press, and despite the long wait period, there is no way to stop the ceiling from crushing you.  This could be forgiven if they were trying to make some sort of statement a la \"The Stanley Parable\", but unfortunately it seems like it's just poorly designed.\n\nIf you press the correct one, you're greeted with a jumping puzzle. Followed by a puzzle no one knows the correct way to solve, but it solves itself anyways if you just spam buttons. Followed by a puzzle where there's a bunch of identical buttons and you just need to keep pressing them all until you find the right one.\n\nThe game continues like this.  At one point there was a \"puzzle\" where you need to input the correct colors on a grid, with seemingly no hints around except for the text \"You are a god\". After struggling with it for several minutes, I gave up and looked up the answer.  Here is the solution from the guide:\n\n[quote]You will get one of two things written on the wall, either “brbrrrbrb” [(the solution)] or “you are a god”. [..] If you get the second prompt, the answer is the same, the game designer is just a jerk and you have no clues to go off of.[/quote]\n\n...Yeah.  You can definitely skip this one.",
